============================================================
10. REQUIREMENT MAPPING
============================================================

Each candidate requirement should have a status:

SUPPORTED
    Evidence directly supports the requirement.

PARTIALLY SUPPORTED
    Some relevant evidence exists.

NOT FOUND
    No relevant evidence was found.

UNCLEAR
    Information exists but requires validation.

NOT APPLICABLE
    Requirement does not apply.

Important:
"Not Found" must NOT be interpreted as "Candidate does not
have this skill."


============================================================
11. EVIDENCE SYSTEM
============================================================

Every important AI insight should be traceable.

Example:

Requirement:
    AWS Experience

Candidate Evidence:
    "Managed AWS infrastructure..."

Source:
    Resume.pdf → Experience section

AI Interpretation:
    Candidate has relevant AWS experience.

The UI must distinguish:
- Original candidate evidence
- AI interpretation
- Human evaluation


============================================================
12. CANDIDATE SUMMARY
============================================================

Generate a structured summary containing:

- Candidate Overview
- Relevant Experience
- Key Skills
- Role Alignment
- Supporting Evidence
- Unclear Information
- Validation Areas
- Interview Focus Areas

AI must not present unsupported assumptions as facts.


============================================================
13. CANDIDATE GROUPING
============================================================

Candidates can be grouped by relevant experience.

Example:
- Strong Backend Experience
- Strong Frontend Experience
- Relevant Domain Experience
- Requires Validation
- Limited Evidence

Groups must have an explainable reason.

Example:
"Grouped because the candidate has explicit Python and backend
experience."


============================================================
14. INTERVIEW INTELLIGENCE
============================================================

HireFlow generates questions based on:

- Job requirements
- Candidate experience
- Existing evidence
- Missing information
- Previously validated areas

Question structure:

Interview Area
    ↓
Primary Question
    ↓
Evidence to Look For
    ↓
Follow-up Question
    ↓
Requirement Being Validated


============================================================
15. FOLLOW-UP QUESTIONS
============================================================

Generate follow-ups when:
- Candidate answer is vague
- Requirement remains unclear
- Evidence conflicts
- Important details are missing
- Interviewer requests deeper validation

Example:

Question:
"Describe a system you designed."

Follow-up:
"What trade-offs influenced your architecture choice?"

Interviewer should be able to manually request a follow-up.


============================================================
16. INTERVIEW NOTES
============================================================

Interview notes should contain:

- Interview area
- Question
- Candidate answer/notes
- Evidence
- Interviewer comments
- Validation status

Notes can be mapped to job requirements.


============================================================
17. INTERVIEW SUMMARY
============================================================

After the interview, generate:

- Key evidence
- Requirements validated
- Partially validated requirements
- Unanswered requirements
- Contradictions
- Additional validation areas

The AI must not make the final hiring decision.


